From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taynotfound <marztayron@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rain-1029: skip the system unmount at power off

T1 (1028): slide to power off stopped at "unmount(0) /", the USB log and
the device went away and the 1027 timer never fired: the kernel itself
wedged in the root's hfs unmount. Skip vfs_unmountall(FALSE) on rain;
sync already ran and the HFS journal replays at the next mount.
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c b/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c
index 51edce0..8281025 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c
@@ -307,9 +307,17 @@ reboot_kernel(int howto, char *message)
 		if (!(howto & RB_PANIC) || !kdp_has_polled_corefile())
 #endif /* DEVELOPMENT || DEBUG */
 		{
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+			/*
+			 * rain: the root's hfs unmount wedged the whole kernel (USB log gone, the 1027 timer never
+			 * ran). The disks were synced above and the HFS journal replays at the next mount.
+			 */
+			printf("RAIN: skipping the system unmount\n");
+#else
 			startTime = mach_absolute_time();
 			vfs_unmountall(FALSE);
 			halt_log_enter("vfs_unmountall", 0, mach_absolute_time() - startTime);
+#endif
 		}
 
 
